# Fixed defect 2379, 2026-11-10, lane b29-pkgmsg, a shape beside it: a file
# of the package `core` calls `mine()`, declared by `<alpha>/a`, which no
# line of `core` names, and by `core`'s own `util`, which `use util` names.
#
# SYMPTOM: `unknown_name` with a near name's rename: only the first module
# in the names' order was asked, `<alpha>/a`, and found out of reach.
#
# FIX: every module declaring the name is asked, and the one a line of the
# file names is offered, `use util`.
use <alpha>/a
use <core>/strings
use <core>/util

function main()
    print(strings.word() + a.mine() + util.mine())
